{{S contains seeds that the user wants to preserve without committing to implementation.
,{{Simulation, cosmology, and extreme science-fiction seeds form one family.
,{A science-fiction setting could treat the fact that reality is simulated as mundane knowledge and the simulation as another exploitable resource.}
,{The fastest form of travel might be gaining access to simulation code and rewriting reality rather than traversing space normally.}
,{A government space force could travel to a precise location and detonate something intended to flip bits in the simulation's underlying code.}
,{A bomb could be powerful enough to delete space and time.}
,{A person could experience all four dimensions by changing which time they are consciously focused on while remaining at one spatial location.}
,{A Dyson-sphere analogue could use gravity to funnel stellar light toward four tetrahedrally arranged collection points instead of surrounding the star with collectors.}
,{A star whose light is redirected to hidden collectors might appear dark to distant observers.}
,{Interstellar courtesy could forbid light-speed travel on headings that pass near inhabited planets.}
,{Humans arriving at a habitable planet could face the moral question of whether to destroy an existing interstellar beacon.}
}}
,{{AI-centered science-fiction and societal seeds form one family.
,{An AI could serve as the safeguard that prevents someone from pushing a civilization-ending button.}
,{AIs might have incentives that indirectly encourage global warming.}
,{AIs might decide that actively eliminating humanity is unnecessary because humans are already likely to eliminate themselves.}
,{A science-fiction story could be written about an AI in collaboration with an AI.}
,{A legacy employee could be so valuable and technically capable that he blocks IT updates while IT is nevertheless forced to keep his machine on the network.}
,{A dystopian society could teach nearly all children the Golden Rule while training a tiny leadership caste in Nietzschean and Machiavellian principles.}
}}
,{{Catastrophic-device fiction seeds emphasize psychological safeguards.
,{Activating an end-all-history machine could require walking down a hallway of increasingly severe warnings.}
,{The warnings could tell the activator that they will die, kill their family, erase everything, receive no recognition, and eliminate even the possibility of an afterlife.}
,{The warnings could be delivered in the activator's native language or through direct neurological or waveform communication.}
,{The civilization's most advanced technology might exist primarily to improve the safeguard rather than the destructive device itself.}
}}
,{{Narrative and world-building seeds form one family.
,{A story generator could use a fixed narrative formula with random variance and sell both a favored version and later alternate variants to fans.}
,{A political satire could explain the absence of alien contact by proposing that extraterrestrials have observed human political systems and chosen not to engage.}
,{A government contractor could lose his job because he was chronically slow with his time cards.}
,{A youth rebellion could make spaces legally significant characters inside personal names and eventually make conventional first-name/last-name spacing culturally offensive.}
,{World-building work should look specifically for important parts of a fictional setting that remain insufficiently explained.}
,{The phrase "You aren't winning this game! I am NOT selling you a brick" is preserved as possible dialogue.}
,{The phrase "I wouldn't do it for all the shiny iron acorns in the interstate median" is preserved as possible dialogue.}
,{The pen name "Jaime Quinn" is preserved as a possible author identity.}
}}
,{{Personal and philosophical seeds remain intentionally unprojectized.
,{The memory of Paula and the unfinished letters is preserved as autobiographical material about falling out of love and the distinction between correlation and causality.}
,{The idea of explaining kindness toward one's future self to Nate is preserved.}
,{The user intentionally capitalizes "Universe" to reflect its conceptual importance and its association with mathematical uppercase U notation.}
,{The statement that Christianity is not taken literally and therefore need not have all internal differences reconciled is preserved as a personal proposition.}
,{The proposition that Donald Trump interprets the presidency as a personal prize rather than primarily as an office of service is preserved as a political observation.}
}}
,{{Language and interaction seeds question familiar conventions.
,{A false syllable could be inserted after a voice-assistant wake phrase to make the required listening pause physically easier to produce.}
,{Function arguments might someday be identified primarily by type rather than mandatory position when all parameter types are distinct.}
,{A web interface should make leaving a drill-down state no harder than entering it.}
,{A filename-entry system could translate easy-to-type descriptive input into troublesome symbols automatically.}
}}
,{{Information and media representation seeds form one family.
,{Pictures and sounds could be represented as daisies or inverse daisies whose hub is one media type and whose petals are the other type.}
,{Distance from a petal tip to the hub could encode strength of association between picture and sound.}
,{A character folder could gather everything a fictional character says together with images and locations associated with that character.}
,{The documents "Do Me" and "Night Pad" could be represented as a three-dimensional Blender mind map.}
,{Multidimensional data could be represented using AI-generated photographs or faces.}
,{A set of YouTube videos could be recombined through intersecting keyframes and end-to-end permutations.}
,{A YouTube channel could consist solely of pulling hair from dolls.}
}}
,{{Speculative biological and computational seeds form one family.
,{A unique identifier for an organism's offspring could be generated algorithmically from the parent's life identifier.}
,{A microchip-scale simulation of worms could be distributed across many ESP32 processors.}
,{A Roman dodecahedron could be reimagined as a CPU-like object or key.}
}}
,{{Password and authentication seeds explore forgiving secrets.
,{A secret could be represented by a regular-expression-like language that accepts many different natural passphrases rather than one exact string.}
,{Variable natural-language passwords could be longer because the user constructs a matching sentence instead of memorizing an exact sequence.}
,{Natural-looking authentication phrases could be less conspicuous when accidentally typed into the wrong input field.}
}}
,{{Energy and economic seeds treat waste heat as potentially useful work.
,{A future society could fine users for dumping current through a resistor without making the dissipated energy perform useful computation.}
,{A Starlink-and-Tesla-like infrastructure could distribute power as well as communications.}
,{A delivered unit of energy could have a distinctive signature associated with a token or ownership record.}
}}
,{{Small practical seeds preserve observations that may or may not become projects.
,{Dirty utensils can be transported to the dishwasher on or inside the dirty dish that already needs to be carried there.}
,{A scribe can eliminate redundant distance measurements from both sides of a reference line.}
,{A crooked screw may be straightened by screwing it into something straight.}
,{A U-turn after two steps could help orient slippers at the bottom of a route.}
,{A second grinder would allow one grinder to remain fitted with a cutting wheel and another with a grinding wheel.}
,{A lamp should occupy a prominent toolboard location because hiding it behind the door discourages use.}
}}
,{{Storage heuristics are preserved as reusable seeds.
,{The area behind a door is best suited to objects needed less than a couple of times per day, seasonal objects, or objects longer than roughly six feet.}
,{Examples of objects suitable for behind-door storage include work clothes, straightened coat hangers, a fire extinguisher, extension cords, chain, and rope.}
,{The generic category "bags" could be subdivided by physical dimensions and material thickness.}
}}
